// @test: typecheck-fail
// @level: L0
// @tier: 0
// @tags: modules, mount, name-resolution, submodule
// @expected-error: E401
//
// Pin (T0795), the control — widening `mount a.b.c;` to mean "the module
// a.b.c" must not make it accept a path that names nothing.
//
// Its sibling `bare_path_mount_of_a_submodule.vr` is passed just as well by a
// branch that stops checking, and this campaign has already measured that
// exact failure twice: a glob whose module does not exist returning Ok, and a
// mount naming a nonexistent item registering nothing and reporting nothing.
// Widening a resolution rule without pinning the rejection is how a gate goes
// vacuous.

mount core.math.frameworks.zz_no_such_module;

fn main() {
    print("ok");
}
